<h2>Retention triggers</h2>
<p>Reach out at scheduled intervals, not when things go wrong.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Day 30:</strong> first traffic update + Google review ask (per <code>/sop/reviews-and-testimonials/</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Month 3:</strong> "what's working / what's missing" check-in. 15 minutes by phone or written.</li>
  <li><strong>Month 6:</strong> half-year QBR (Quarterly Business Review). Walk through analytics, lead quality, what's next.</li>
  <li><strong>Month 12:</strong> annual review. Discuss any roadmap items, refresh the seasonal pages, plan year ahead.</li>
  <li><strong>Annually after:</strong> repeat the 12-month pattern.</li>
</ul>

<h2>QBR template (month 6 + annual)</h2>
<p>30-45 minute call. Agenda:</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Traffic recap.</strong> Visits, top pages, conversion path, mobile / desktop split. Pull from the dashboard.</li>
  <li><strong>Lead recap.</strong> Forms submitted, calls received (if tracked), best-performing landing pages or service pages.</li>
  <li><strong>What is missing.</strong> Open question to the client. Often surfaces upsell opportunities.</li>
  <li><strong>What I am shipping next.</strong> 1-2 small improvements I will make in the next 30 days. Demonstrates the work continues.</li>
  <li><strong>Roadmap.</strong> Anything on their wish list that has a clear scope.</li>
</ol>

